                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 22 at 5:54PM MDT until September 22 at 7:30PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "...FLASH FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 730 PM MDT THIS\nEVENING FOR SOUTHWESTERN MORA COUNTY...\n\nAt 554 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 3 and 6 inches of rain have\nfallen. A report of 5.89 inches of rain has been recorded at the JTH\nForestry Center in Mora. Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.25\ninches are possible in the warned area. Significant flash flooding is\nalready occurring in Monte Aplanado and Mora. Highway 94 is also\nflooded and impassible south of Mora.\n\nFLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY for Mora, Monte Aplanado, Canon and Ledoux as\nwell as the Rito Cebolla. This is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS\nSITUATION. SEEK HIGHER GROUND NOW!\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...This is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER\nGROUND NOW! Life threatening flash flooding of low water\ncrossings, small creeks and streams, urban areas, highways,\nstreets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMora, Ledoux, Morphy Lake State Park, Monte Aplanado and\nGolondrinas.\n\nThis includes State Road 518 between Mile Markers 19 and 21...and\nnear Mile Marker 29.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas...\nMorphy Lake State Park.\n\nFlash flooding is also expected in the Rito Cebolla. Stay away from\nriver banks.",
                "instruction": "Move to higher ground now! This is an extremely dangerous and\nlife-threatening situation. Do not attempt to travel unless you are\nfleeing an area subject to flooding or under an evacuation order.\n\nIn hilly or mountainous terrain there are numerous low water\ncrossings which are potentially dangerous in heavy rain. Do not\nattempt to cross flooded roads. Find an alternate route.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFSABQ"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS75 KABQ 222354"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
                        "FLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY FOR MORA, MONTE APLANADO, CANON AND LEDOUX AS WELL AS THE RITO CEBOLLA"
                    ],
